Description: Upload-only cloud folder (Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox, ...)
 CloudDrop uploads everything you put in ~/CloudDrop to your cloud, with the
 same folder structure: Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox, Nextcloud or another
 WebDAV server, S3-compatible storage, SFTP or MEGA. Deleting a file on your
 computer never deletes it in the cloud: it becomes cloud-only and can be
 downloaded back at any time, so you can free up space without losing
 anything. Space can also be freed automatically some days after upload, and
 several folders can each upload to a cloud of their own.
 .
 It includes a desktop app with a setup assistant, a file browser and an
 activity history, a top-bar status icon, status icons and actions in GNOME
 Files, and a background service that resumes interrupted uploads.
